{"seq":15,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/hermes-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T00:33:51.719Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"35809440614777ea3bdd688df6a6513f43686265525c267f43e8e8d444d5fe7f","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"#coastal-team","text":"Bettina, here's what I found in #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal notes.\n\nPellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL, Gulf Coast)\n- #4419: Yard_Dwell_Summary report times out when filtered by container length. Open. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. See the caveat below.\n- PD-8841: how Pemberline Dock handles chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (Gate 4B). Source: your own Dec 2025 cutover recap, not a channel or one of Moss's notes. I included it because it's PHL.\n\nDriftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)\n- Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, asked for by their warehouse managers. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n- #4419 may also belong here. Moss's 11/2/2025 digest lists #4419 as a barge slip 7 schedule sync ticket on Kwame's port account, with Driftmoor asking for a patched manifest CSV. Same number, two different issues and two different accounts.\n- No ticket number: the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B, and engineering gave a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. Source: cheat sheet.\n\nPlease confirm #4419 with Kwame. I can't tell from the notes whether it is the PHL report timeout, the DMF slip sync, or two tickets that share a number.\n\nLeft out as Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark: PD-4821 and #8812. Also left out as other accounts: PD-4827 and PD-4824 (Saltmarsh).\n\nI found nothing on either account in #coastal-team or #coastal-random themselves. I can't see account ticket folders, so the CRM or support system may hold tickets that aren't in these notes.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":